<title>CHINA: Shanghai Kaikai 96 net up 80.04 pct.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Kaikai 96 net up 80.04 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of yuan unless stated, against 1995 figures)</p>
<p> Turnover	   327.451		 vs     317.594</p>
<p> Net profit	  60.175		 vs     33.424</p>
<p> Net asset per share     1.880 yuan   vs     1.644</p>
<p> Earnings per share	0.304 yuan   vs     0.363</p>
<p>(The company listed its B shares on January 8, 1997)</p>
<p>Company name: Shanghai Kaikai Industrial Co Ltd</p>
<p>Note: the results were published in a company statement. The figures are based on domestic accounting standards. Figures based on international accounting standards were not available.</p>
<p>The company's board of directors proposed no cash dividend or bonus issue for B shareholders and a cash dividend of 0.15 yuan per share for other shareholders, pending approval of a shareholders' meeting.</p>
</text>
